  "details": "In an Animator Tracking Control, when only the fingers are set to \"Tracking\" (while the rest is still set to \"Animation\"), the tracking will resume only for the local player. \n\nRemote players will see the fingers still frozen (they will move for one frame and freeze again)\n\nHowever, the tracking will be seen by other players if at least one upper body part is set to Tracking (head,Hip,left arm or right arm)\n\nReproducable: (only tested with Index)\n\n-Animation Controller in Slot \"Action\"\n\n-Create Layer with humanoid animation, add an Animator Tracking Control to set everything to \"animation\" (except jaw/eyes)\n\n-Create another layer with a state that has an \"Animator Tracking Control\" attribute\n\n-Set left & right fingers to Tracking\n\n= Fingers will start being tracked again, BUT only locally, other players will see it move for a frame and then freeze again",
